    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0027" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.24/349²⁄₁₂: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-07T09:00:00+03:00">May 7, 1942—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 7—8:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>727. My 717, May 6, 9 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">a.m</hi>.] The Middle East
                    Supply Center received a telegram from London indicating that [a representative]
                    from the Maxwell Mission and a civilian sent from Washington are to be American
                    representatives in the Center. The message adds that until the latter arrives an
                    officer will be [designated] from this Legation to serve in his stead. This
                    appears to dispose of the questions raised in my telegram referred to.</p>
                <pb facs="0028" n="16" xml:id="pg16"/>
                <p>Invitations to attend the Council meetings next week either in person or by
                    alternate are about to be issued to General Maxwell and Jacobs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
